 "rules": [
  "Each entry of runs is one honest run's expected inputs, with exactly the keys of TABLE.md §4.1. A plant run's expected inputs are its world's honest run's (TABLE.md §8.1), but for plant_inputs_changed.",
  "Every number is SPEC.md's binary64 literal as written (SPEC:104), written in Python's repr form. The judge compares numbers as binary64 values, so 602214076 and 602214076.0 are equal.",
  "Lists are compared as sets of members, matched by id, by ligand and node (free_amounts) or by patch and ligand (permeabilities); ligands and observation_times_s as sets of values (TABLE.md §4.1).",
  "A null is a value this file does not fix, one of TABLE.md §4.1's exceptions: constants.RT_pJ_per_fmol (recorded, since SPEC gives RT as a formula); W1eq's start; W6's unregistered cell. The notes say which.",
  "multipliers holds {\"each_value\": 1.0}: SPEC names no multiplier, so every member the engine lists must have that value (SPEC:62). It is the one key whose expected form differs from the echo's.",
  "A trace (declared false) is 1e-12 mM times its compartment's volume_pL, in binary64 (SPEC:104-105; TABLE.md §4.1). At every registered volume that product is exact.",
  "permeabilities lists every ligand on every patch at 0.0 (SPEC:59-61); charges every ligand at 0 (SPEC:59).",
  "plant_inputs_changed holds W1p-P2's two crossed k_off, each the other population's registered value. They apply only if P2 is planted by declaration; otherwise W1p-P2's inputs_changed is empty and its inputs equal W1p's. Every other plant's inputs_changed is empty, unless a dated addendum names a list (TABLE.md §8.1).",
  "Before any registered run the judge cross-checks this file against the references' world echo, by TABLE.md §4.1's key map. A departure stops the judge before anything is scored."
